Priests may have too low 'Int' to learn new spells, specifically not the
high level spells like magic mapping. With an Int:7 and XL:3 you fail to
read even a level 1 spellbook with rate of 50%. With XL:6 it's still only
60% success. With XL:6 and Int:10 only 75% success rate for level 1 books
and only 35% success for a level 5 spellbook like magic mapping. They can
quite reliably cast _known_ spells with their robe. (They can of course
make use of their spare holy water to bless a book before reading. But
you'd want to do that only if you know the book, if you have previously
identified it.)

I also doubt that:
"Priests can start with (and be able to cast on the first turn of the game)
 [spells listed are mentioned subsequently]"

With Wis:18 you have at XL:1 (with robe, and without shield, etc.):
* healing, protection, create monster, light, remove curse  --  0% failure
* identify, stone to flesh                                  -- 79% failure
* create familiar, detect treasure, magic mapping           -- 93% failure

> 
> 8. The Priest quest is easy, the nemesis is easy, the quest is chocked full
> of chests with all manner of treasures and you can lead wraiths to the
> upstairs to defeat them so that they leave a corpse. Because of this,
> priests can reach level 30 faster than any other role. The quest artifact
> is good (not awesome, it doesn't give magic resistance) and it's an
> acension kit piece (helm of brilliance). Unlike other quests it's not
> necessary to have reflection or magic resistance.

I don't think it's necessary to become XL:30; you may even want to avoid
it given that more high level monsters will be generated then. (In my last
five ascended priests I had XL: 22, 19, 30, 24, 21.)

The quest is easy if you take precautions; on the locate level I typically
burn a permanent E-word on the stairs to avoid the [rare] level drains.
(You wouldn't engrave the E-word if you want the wraiths follow you up.
But mind that all those levels have morgues; so to get the corpses from
wraith luring would require to take all the wraiths out of the quest.)

And I also recall that the hostile priest on the locate level is very tough,
so a bit care is necessary.

